  "title": "RBI's Liquidity Mop-Up and India's Economic Challenges",
  "summary": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) continues its liquidity mop-up efforts to stabilize the rupee amid rising crude oil prices and geopolitical tensions, while India's trade deficit widened to $31.98 billion in Q1FY27, partially offset by growth in exports of petroleum products, electronics, engineering, and marine goods. The Indian government emphasizes wage growth to boost consumption and is addressing business disputes through dialogue and transparency.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The RBI absorbed Rs 1.91 trillion through liquidity mop-up auctions, increasing demand for liquidity amid surplus reserves.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
